\section{Executive Summary}

A comprehensive Vulnerability Assessment and Penetration Testing (VAPT) engagement was conducted on the VajraKavach platform, a secure job search and professional networking application. The assessment covered the full stack: FastAPI backend, React frontend, nginx reverse proxy, PostgreSQL database, and end-to-end encryption subsystem.

\subsection{Scope}
\begin{itemize}[nosep]
  \item \textbf{Backend:} FastAPI (Python 3.10), REST API endpoints, authentication, authorization
  \item \textbf{Frontend:} React 18 + Vite, client-side E2E encryption (RSA-2048 + AES-256-GCM)
  \item \textbf{Infrastructure:} nginx 1.18, TLS 1.3, PostgreSQL 14
  \item \textbf{Testing Types:} Static code analysis, dynamic testing, dependency CVE scanning
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Methodology}
Testing followed the OWASP Testing Guide v4.2 and OWASP Top 10 (2021) frameworks:
\begin{enumerate}[nosep]
  \item Static source code review across all backend routes, middleware, services, and frontend utilities
  \item Dynamic testing of live endpoints including header analysis, CORS, JWT attacks, brute force, IDOR, and injection payloads
  \item Automated dependency vulnerability scanning using \texttt{pip-audit} and \texttt{npm audit}
\end{enumerate}

\subsection{Summary of Findings}

\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{|>{\columncolor{critical}\color{white}\bfseries}c|>{\columncolor{high}\color{white}\bfseries}c|>{\columncolor{medium}\color{white}\bfseries}c|>{\columncolor{low}\color{white}\bfseries}c|>{\columncolor{info}\color{white}\bfseries}c|}
