\section{Positive Security Controls}

The following security measures were found to be correctly implemented:

\begin{itemize}[nosep]
  \item \textbf{TLS 1.3} with AES-256-GCM cipher suite and HSTS headers
  \item \textbf{Argon2id} password hashing with proper parameters
  \item \textbf{TOTP-based 2FA} mandatory for all users
  \item \textbf{JWT IP binding} prevents token reuse from different IPs
  \item \textbf{E2E encryption} using RSA-4096 OAEP + AES-256-GCM hybrid scheme
  \item \textbf{PBKDF2} with 250,000 iterations for client-side key derivation
  \item \textbf{Resume encryption at rest} using Fernet (AES-128-CBC + HMAC-SHA256)
  \item \textbf{Digital signatures} for resume integrity verification (PKI)
  \item \textbf{Blockchain audit logging} for immutable action tracking
  \item \textbf{CORS origin validation} correctly rejects unauthorized origins
  \item \textbf{Rate limiting} at 60 req/min global, 15 req/min on auth endpoints
  \item \textbf{LAN-only access} restricted to 192.168.3.0/24 via nginx
  \item \textbf{Token type enforcement} prevents refresh tokens from being used as access tokens
  \item \textbf{JWT revocation} via in-memory blocklist on logout and token refresh
  \item \textbf{Security headers:} X-Frame-Options, X-Content-Type-Options, HSTS, CSP, Referrer-Policy, Permissions-Policy
  \item \textbf{SQLAlchemy ORM} prevents SQL injection via parameterized queries
  \item \textbf{Request ID tracing} for audit and forensic trail
  \item \textbf{User report/flag system} for abuse prevention
\end{itemize}

% =====================================================================
\section{Conclusion}

The VajraKavach platform demonstrates strong security architecture with multiple layers of defense. Across two rounds of assessment, 42 vulnerabilities were identified and 32 were remediated, with 6 accepted risks documented with rationale. All Critical and High severity findings that were fixable without infrastructure changes (Redis) have been resolved.

Key improvements from the re-audit include: token type enforcement, admin privilege escalation prevention, IP spoofing mitigation, IDOR remediation, account enumeration elimination, and LAN-only access restriction.

The platform achieves a \textbf{STRONG} overall security posture, suitable for deployment within the IIIT-Delhi network environment with the implemented mitigations. The remaining accepted risks are documented and appropriate for the LAN-only threat model.

